    "description": "Companion data for the notebook *Squares in Squares: bands, gadgets, exact angles*.\n\n**submission.csv** - a complete, verifier-certified submission for the Kaggle competition *Squares in Squares* (pack n unit squares, n = 1..1000, into the smallest enclosing square). It merges the best public packings, dilates every packing by 1 + 1e-10 so that exact irrational contacts pass the interval-arithmetic verifier, and adds one packing composed by a fault-line gadget search (n = 654). Public score 22.2619751.\n\n**perpuzzle_best.csv** - the best side length L reached on the leaderboard for every puzzle n, with the team and date, as published by the competition hosts in their per-puzzle leaderboard notebook.\n\n**targets.csv** - for every n >= 325 written as n = K^2 + D: our overhang f = L - K, the leaders' overhang, and the score gap (L_ours - L_best) / sqrt(n). This is the table behind the gap analysis in the notebook.\n\nColumns of submission.csv follow the competition format: id (n_square_id), n, square_id, x, y, angle (radians).",
